.TH SIMRV 1 "September 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv \- Dual-width explainable RISC-V architectural simulator and TUI workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B SimRV
[\fB\-\-cli\fR]
[\fB\-\-ca\fR|\fB\-\-ia\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fIelf_file\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIsteps\fR]
[\fB\-\-cpu\-profile\fR \fIcfg_file\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SimRV
is an explainable, dual-width (RV32 / RV64) RISC-V architectural simulator featuring an interactive terminal workbench (TUI), cycle-accurate microarchitectural modeling, hardware RTL parity verification, and full-system SMP Linux emulation.
.PP
When invoked without arguments or with an ELF file, \fBSimRV\fR launches the interactive TUI workbench by default. Pass \fB\-\-cli\fR for headless batch or scripted execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Execution Interface"
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cli
Force headless command-line execution (disables the TUI workbench).
.TP
.BR \-\-tui
Force interactive terminal user interface workbench (default).
.SS "Simulation Engine & Microarchitecture"
.TP
.BR \-\-ca
Select cycle-accurate pipeline simulation kernel.
.TP
.BR \-\-ia
Select high-speed instruction-accurate simulation kernel.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pipeline " " \fItype\fR
Select pipeline microarchitecture target (\fBthree-stage\fR, \fBfive-stage\fR, or \fBdual-issue\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-cpu\-profile " " \fIpath.cfg\fR
Load a human-editable CPU microarchitecture profile (.cfg).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-e ", " \-\-steps " " \fIN\fR
Stop simulation after \fIN\fR total instructions have retired across all harts.
.SS "Memory & Kernel Loading"
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-memory " " \fIfile.elf\fR
Load a bare-metal ELF binary into guest physical memory.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-tohost " " \fIaddr\fR
Specify physical address of the \fBtohost\fR communication symbol.
.TP
.BR \-\-kernel " " \fIpath\fR
Load Linux kernel binary image (full-system mode).
.TP
.BR \-\-disk " " \fIpath.img\fR
Attach virtual disk image via VirtIO Block device.
.TP
.BR \-\-smp " " \fIN\fR
Configure number of active SMP harts (2 to 16; default: 1 for single-hart).
.TP
.BR \-\-ram " " \fIMB\fR
Configure guest RAM capacity in megabytes (default: 2048 MB).
.SS "Debugging & Tracing"
.TP
.BR \-\-trace
Write architectural execution trace to \fItrace/trace.txt\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-tracepc
Write PC instruction stream to \fItrace/tracepc.txt\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-gdb
Start GDB Remote Serial Protocol (RSP) target server.
.TP
.BR \-\-gdb\-port " " \fIport\fR
Specify TCP port for GDB RSP server (default: 1234).
.SS "General Information"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print simulator version and build metadata.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line options and exit.
.SH TUI WORKBENCH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.BR [Space]
Pause or resume simulation execution. Input routes to the guest terminal while running and to TUI navigation while paused.
.TP
.BR [n] ", " [F3]
Step execution by one machine cycle across all harts.
.TP
.BR [r]
Run simulation continuously.
.TP
.BR [Tab]
Cycle active visualizer tabs (Regs, Cache, TLB, Pipeline, Hazards, Explainer).
.TP
.BR [q]
Quit the simulator.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv\-cpu\-wizard (1),
.BR simrv\-tune (1),
.BR simrv\-parity (1),
.BR simrv\-benchmark (1)
.PP
